{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And they shall say to me, What is His name? — מה</b> The ס\"ת (sum of the verse's ends) is שם, a name of ד' letters that HaShem transmitted to him, and written immediately after it: Go and gather the elders of Israel — for it is transmitted only to the elders of the generation. Three times אהיה, corresponding to the three patriarchs, and they are Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob. Abraham: והיה ברכה. Isaac: גור בארץ הזאת ואהיה עמך. Jacob: שוב אל ארץ אבותיך ואהיה עמך. אהיה ascends כ\"א, and likewise the beginning of the three names of the י\"ג attributes: ה' ה' אל, and likewise ר\"ת of אברהם יצחק ויעקב, and likewise the beginning of the חומשי תורה: ב' ו' ו' ו' א'. אהיה appears ב\"פ, ascending in calculation מ\"ב — He transmitted to him a name of מ\"ב letters. Three times אהי\"ה ascend ס\"ג, and they are י\"ב letters corresponding to the י\"ב tribes, and the tribes are נ' letters. Combine with them the י\"ג letters of the names of the patriarchs, and the total is ס\"ג."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "In the phrase 'והיה ברכה' (Genesis 12:2), the word 'אהיה' does not appear in that verse; the linkage appears to rest on the shared root היה. The phrase 'גור בארץ הזאת ואהיה עמך' combines elements from Genesis 26:3; the verse contains 'גור בארץ הזאת' and 'ואהיה עמך' is in Genesis 28:15 (Jacob). For 'אהיה עולה בחשבון מ\"ב': the word אהיה = 21; it appears twice (ב\"פ) in the verse; 21 × 2 = 42 = מ\"ב. The claim 'ג\"פ אהי\"ה עולה ס\"ג' refers to three occurrences of אהיה across the three patriarchal verses, 21 × 3 = 63 = ס\"ג."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:12:06.214858428Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}